Cryptographic origin
--------------------
crypto/ed25519.c and crypto/ed25519.h preserve their declared lineage from
TweetNaCl v20140427 through SigilOS to Beyond. The original TweetNaCl code
is public domain. Its upstream contributors are Daniel J. Bernstein,
Bernard van Gastel, Wesley Janssen, Tanja Lange, Peter Schwabe and Sjaak
Smetsers. The source comments retain the lineage and credit the original
implementation; BSD-3-Clause covers Fermi Hart's adaptations and maintenance.
See LICENSES/LicenseRef-TweetNaCl-Public-Domain.txt for the upstream notice.

Runtime and build tools
-----------------------
The sovereign build incorporates the explicitly supplied Beyond blibc
archive and startup code under Unlicense, plus the Beyond runtime shim
and linker script under their preserved SPL context. Their identities
are recorded in the build receipt. These external inputs are not
relicensed by changing the Basm project license.

NASM is an external test oracle. NASM, host compilers, system libc, Bear
and BearLinker are not distributed as separate tools in the Basm package.

Source origin
-------------
provenance/UPSTREAM.json identifies the Beyond revision from which the
assembler sources were adapted. It is an origin reference, not a manifest
of the current tree or a build receipt. The preserved comparison fixture
quarantine/basm_monolith_legacy.c supports regression and benchmark tools;
it is not an active assembler input. Current build instructions are in
docs/BUILD.md.
